  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection of Vulnerable Conflict-Affected Communities in Ukraine and Provision of Urgent Mental Health and Psychosocial Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over eight months into the war, millions of people in Ukraine remain in need of humanitarian assistance. The recent wave of attacks on essential civilian infrastructure has worsened living conditions in large parts of the country, where the availability of water, heating and power utilities is now precarious. The dramatic deterioration of the situation may impact mobility dynamics, exposing people to heightened protection risks, and negatively affecting their mental health and psychosocial well-being. Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to safe, dignified conditions and principled mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) and protection assistance for the war-affected populations in Ukraine. IOM is also extending its commitment to protect affected populations from sexual exploitation and abuse (SEA) across all project activities. To empower local organizations, IOM is equipping four civil society organizations (CSOs) to deliver community-based psychosocial activities.</narrative>
  </description>
